<title>BRAZIL: Brazil deputy to present final oil law draft Tues.</title>
<headline>Brazil deputy to present final oil law draft Tues.</headline>
<dateline>BRASILIA 1997-01-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>A final draft of a bill regulating the opening up of Brazil's oil and gas monopoly to the private sector was due to be presented to a Chamber of Deputies committee on Tuesday, an official said.</p>
<p>Lawmakers may propose changes to the bill during a further five sessions of the panel before it is put to a vote which, if approved, advances to the floor of the Chamber of Deputies, an aide to Dep. Eliseu Resende, who drew up the draft, said.</p>
<p>The bill does not contemplate the privatization of oil and gas monopoly Petrobras but instead lays down rules for competition between the state giant and the private sector.</p>
<p>((-- William Schomberg, Brasilia newsroom 5561 2230358))</p>
